+// parse_vector by tiles (#2536): the kernels and the fallback over one run of top-level declarations of about
+// `tile_tokens` tokens at a time (parse_tile_end), each as a unit of its own whose type names from the tiles before it are
+// marked as clang's predeclared ones are, so that the kernels' temporaries are a tile's, which stays in the cache, and
+// the tree's columns are written a tile at a time. A tile's tokens are a unit's to every kernel: the columns' entries
+// around it hold what a unit's padding holds while its kernels run, and its parents are counted from its first token
+// until they are done. A top-level declaration parses alone as it does in its unit, given the type names before it
+// (the fallback's rule, parse_fallback_item), so the tree is the unit's. A tile the kernels or the fallback can't take
+// (as a unit they can't, or a tile cut short) sends the unit to parse_vector as one.
